So story is awesome.

00:25:13.920 --> 00:25:18.683
Let me just go through the three types
of qualities that companies that

00:25:18.683 --> 00:25:20.306
harness story well do.

00:25:20.306 --> 00:25:25.672
They tend to harness story
in a way that really designs

00:25:25.672 --> 00:25:30.930
story with authenticity,
empathy, and purpose.

00:25:30.930 --> 00:25:34.300
So, first, design for authenticity.

00:25:34.300 --> 00:25:39.533
When you share a story, if you're a CEO,
you're starting a company,

00:25:39.533 --> 00:25:44.433
you're trying to recruit, retain so
you need to feel authentic.

00:25:44.433 --> 00:25:49.235
Research by Body shows that people can
tell within milliseconds of meeting

00:25:49.235 --> 00:25:53.419
you whether they trust you, like you,
whether you're authentic, and

00:25:53.419 --> 00:25:57.626
that type of science applies when
you're especially sharing stories.

00:25:57.626 --> 00:26:02.870
And both customers and employees need to
believe your story and be inspired by it.

00:26:02.870 --> 00:26:06.610
And what's happening right now
in the world is that brands and

00:26:06.610 --> 00:26:11.010
organizations and companies often
feel manufactured but people don't.

00:26:11.010 --> 00:26:14.654
So one of the reasons story's
become this kind of bigger thing or

00:26:14.654 --> 00:26:19.330
this notion of people as brands has become
a bigger thing is partly because of that

00:26:19.330 --> 00:26:23.200
deep desire to have authenticity and
trust in our relationships.

